[Music]  fans around the world are eagerly  awaiting the release of the batman but  the film won't be coming to russian  cinemas why not and how do people feel  about it keep watching to find out the  release of a new batman movie is always  a major film industry event undoubtedly  so when it changes the franchise's  direction in a significant manner or  even better marks the debut of a brand  new actor donning the cape the cowl and  the kevlar armor matt reeves the batman  checks all those boxes and more this  detective noir approach is markedly  different from zack snyder's more  action-oriented batman and robert  battenson's young slightly diy-caped  crusader is a considerable departure  from ben affleck's buff grizzled and  aging dark knight  well  here i am  the movie's casting is also a far cry  from your typical hollywood fair  pattinson paul dano who plays a riddler  and zoe kravitz who plays catwoman may  be no strangers to major motion pictures  but they come with plenty of indie  credibility to go with their requisite  dramatic accomplishments meanwhile  arguably the biggest traditional movie  star in the film colin farrell plays the  penguin under a mountain of makeup and  prosthetics as such there are plenty of  fans who can't wait for the movie's  release both in the us and other  countries it's one of the major  characters of the 20th century and so  many people connect it on such a deep  level and for so many different reasons  in fact with the movie cleared for  release in china the batman might have a  decent chance to become a massive global  super hit a rare feat in this day and  age however there's one market that  won't get to enjoy the movie and it's  jaw-dropping run time because the batman  won't be available in russian movie  theaters let's take a look at the  reasons behind this omission the reason  the batman won't make an appearance in  russian cinemas and the foreseeable  future is a country's invasion of  ukraine according to cnn business this  isn't a logistical issue either the  film's distributor specifically made the  decision to pull the movie the  announcement is one of the most high  profile among the several recent  entertainment industry decisions to take  business away from russia a spokesperson  for the company said in light of the  humanitarian crisis in ukraine warner  media is pausing the release of its  feature film the batman in russia we  will continue to monitor the situation  as it evolves it remains to be seen how  the situation develops but the warner  media spokesperson expressed the  company's wish of how it should wrap up  adding we hope for a swift and peaceful  resolution to this tragedy the latest  developments of the batman and this  russian release or rather lack thereof  have been noted in the people's court of  social media and multiple twitter users  have spoken their minds about the  situation though people appreciate or at  the very least understand the decision  there are different opinions about its  meaningfulness and effectiveness some  people have been quick to show their  support one twitter user wrote the  batman film release is on hold for  russia good moral principle over profits  even in hard times good for warner  brothers another user thought along the  same lines saying i congratulate warner  brothers for pulling out of distributing  in russia what is touted as their  blockbuster of the year the movie the  batman others however were more  skeptical of the move and pointed out  that pausing a movie's release isn't  likely to have a major impact in the  grand scheme of things one doubtful  person sarcastically tweeted that'll  stop them movie companies are really  acting like the batman not releasing in  russia is going to make putin stop  thanks to its impending release date of  the batman and the massive hype  surrounding it warner brothers pulling  the movie from russia is arguably the  hardest immediate blow to the country's  movie theaters however it's far from the  only hit russia has taken from the  entertainment industry as of late in  fact multiple entertainment juggernauts  have made similar decisions on the  streaming side of things netflix  recently refused to add state mandated  content on its platform in russia  according to deadline similarly disney's  release sports in the country means  titles like dr strange and the  multiverse of madness might not see a  russian release sony will do the same  with morbius as well as the other movies  that have planned to release in the  country  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

